  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated AIDS Programme, Thika</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 2-year project continues the work of the Integrated AIDS Program in its efforts towards the prevention and control of the spread of HIV and AIDS and the provision of care and support services to people living with and affected by HIV, in the Gatundu North district of Kiambu county. It does this through community sensitisation on HIV prevention and on strategies of coping with the effects of HIV and AIDS through awareness campaigns, HIV Testing and Counselling (HTC) services, Education For Life (EFL) activities, care and support for infected and affected persons. In addition, the project focuses on the needs of Orphans and Vulnerable Children (OVCs), through provision of school fees and other education support; apprenticeships and training on improved farming methods; promotion of income-generating activities; monitoring and supervision, and capacity-building. 

IAP plans to empower the community in better farming methods, economic sustainability and wealth creation strategies which will equip the community with the capacity to improve their skills on soil and water conservation and planting of drought resistant crops. These strategies will ensure that households in the community have sustainable food supply. The programme will also engage the community into poverty reduction through micro finance and agri-business as a way of promoting asset acquisition for the households, increased income and sustainable financial stability.</narrative>
  </description>
